 related to Order. A query must return customers with at least one order this month. Which records capability helps?","options":["Filtering on related record fields in the query","A group","A constant","Querying all customers and all orders separately and matching in the interface"],"explanation":"Relationships allow filtering on related record fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type de Contrato debe mostrar en la lista un indicador \"Vence pronto\" para los contratos que caducan en menos de 30 días. ¿Qué capacidad encaja sin cambiar la tabla?","options":["Un filtro de usuario","Un campo personalizado calculado con la condición de fecha","Una columna nueva en la tabla actualizada cada noche por un proceso","Un grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los campos personalizados calculados derivan valores de otros campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Contract record type must show a \"Expiring soon\" indicator in the list for contracts expiring within 30 days. Which capability fits without changing the table?","options":["A user filter","A calculated custom field with the date condition","A new table column updated nightly by a process","A group"],"explanation":"Calculated custom fields derive values from other fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene definir al configurar las columnas de la lista de un record type? (Elige 2)","options":["Si las columnas permiten ordenar","Las contraseñas de los usuarios","Qué campos se muestran","El esquema de la base de datos","Los permisos de los process models"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Las columnas definen qué se muestra y cómo se ordena.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements should be defined when configuring a record type's list columns? (Choose 2)","options":["Whether columns are sortable","User passwords","Which fields are shown","The database schema","Process model permissions"],"explanation":"Columns define what's shown and how it's sorted."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que una vista de registro solo la vean los gestores. ¿Qué configura?","options":["Un proceso","Un filtro por defecto","La visibilidad de esa vista para el grupo de gestores","Una validación en la interfaz de la vista que muestre un error a los demás"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las vistas de registro admiten condiciones de visibilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants a record view visible only to managers. What do they configure?","options":["A process","A default filter","That view's visibility for the managers group","A validation in the view's interface showing an error to others"],"explanation":"Record views support visibility conditions."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro se abre desde la lista y el usuario quiere volver a la lista con los mismos filtros. ¿Qué ventaja ofrece usar la lista de registros estándar?","options":["Navegación integrada entre lista y registro","Ninguna","Que no necesita permisos","Que los filtros se guardan en la base de datos de la aplicación"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La experiencia de records integra la navegación entre lista y vistas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record is opened from the list and the user wants to return to the list with the same filters. What advantage does the standard record list offer?","options":["Built-in navigation between list and record","None","No permissions needed","Filters being saved to the application's database"],"explanation":"The records experience integrates navigation between list and views."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve la expresión sum({4, 6, 10})?","options":["{4, 6, 10}","3","20","10"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"sum suma los elementos de la lista: 4 + 6 + 10 = 20.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the expression sum({4, 6, 10}) return?","options":["{4, 6, 10}","3","20","10"],"explanation":"sum adds the list items: 4 + 6 + 10 = 20."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve if(ri!importe > 1000, \"Alta\", \"Normal\") cuando ri!importe es 500?","options":["Un error","null","\"Normal\"","\"Alta\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La condición es falsa, así que devuelve el tercer argumento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does if(ri!amount > 1000, \"High\", \"Normal\") return when ri!amount is 500?","options":["An error","null","\"Normal\"","\"High\""],"explanation":"The condition is false, so it returns the third argument."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve index({\"rojo\", \"verde\", \"azul\"}, 2, null)?","options":["\"azul\"","2","\"rojo\"","\"verde\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"En Appian los índices empiezan en 1: el segundo elemento es \"verde\".","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index({\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\"}, 2, null) return?","options":["\"blue\"","2","\"red\"","\"green\""],"explanation":"Appian indexes start at 1: the second item is \"green\"."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * 10)?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","10","60","{10, 20, 30}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!forEach aplica la expresión a cada elemento y devuelve una lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * 10) return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","10","60","{10, 20, 30}"],"explanation":"a!forEach applies the expression to each item and returns a list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve length({\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"})?","options":["1","\"abcd\"","4","3"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"length devuelve el número de elementos de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does length({\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}) return?","options":["1","\"abcd\"","4","3"],"explanation":"length returns the number of list items."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve wherecontains(\"b\", {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"b\"})?","options":["{2, 4}","{\"b\", \"b\"}","2","true"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"wherecontains devuelve los índices donde aparece el valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does wherecontains(\"b\", {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"b\"}) return?","options":["{2, 4}","{\"b\", \"b\"}","2","true"],"explanation":"wherecontains returns the indexes where the value appears."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve joinarray({\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}, \", \")?","options":["\"Ana, Luis, Eva\"","\"AnaLuisEva\"","{\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}","3"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"joinarray une los elementos con el separador indicado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does joinarray({\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}, \", \") return?","options":["\"Ana, Luis, Eva\"","\"AnaLuisEva\"","{\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}","3"],"explanation":"joinarray joins items with the given separator."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve append({1, 2}, 3)?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{3, 1, 2}","6","{1, 2}"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"append añade el valor al final de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does append({1, 2}, 3) return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{3, 1, 2}","6","{1, 2}"],"explanation":"append adds the value at the end of the list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve \"Hola \" & \"mundo\" en una expresión de Appian?","options":["{\"Hola \", \"mundo\"}","\"Hola mundo\"","true","Un error, porque & solo sirve para valores booleanos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El operador & concatena textos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does \"Hello \" & \"world\" return in an Appian expression?","options":["{\"Hello \", \"world\"}","\"Hello world\"","true","An error, because & only works with booleans"],"explanation":"The & operator concatenates text."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve and(true, false)?","options":["null","Un error","false","true"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"and devuelve true solo si todos los argumentos son verdaderos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does and(true, false) return?","options":["null","An error","false","true"],"explanation":"and returns true only if every argument is true."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve or(false, true, false)?","options":["{false, true, false}","true","null","false"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"or devuelve true si al menos un argumento es verdadero.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does or(false, true, false) return?","options":["{false, true, false}","true","null","false"],"explanation":"or returns true if at least one argument is true."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve max({7, 3, 12, 5})?","options":["27","3","4","12"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"max devuelve el valor más alto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does max({7, 3, 12, 5}) return?","options":["27","3","4","12"],"explanation":"max returns the highest value."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve contains({10, 20, 30}, 20)?","options":["false","true","2","20"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"contains indica si el valor está en la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does contains({10, 20, 30}, 20) return?","options":["false","true","2","20"],"explanation":"contains indicates whether the value is in the list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!match(value: \"B\", equals: \"A\", then: 1, equals: \"B\", then: 2, default: 0)?","options":["1","0","2","\"B\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!match devuelve el then del primer caso que coincide.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!match(value: \"B\", equals: \"A\", then: 1, equals: \"B\", then: 2, default: 0) return?","options":["1","0","2","\"B\""],"explanation":"a!match returns the then of the first matching case."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!isNullOrEmpty({})?","options":["null","0","true","false"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Una lista vacía se considera vacía.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!isNullOrEmpty({}) return?","options":["null","0","true","false"],"explanation":"An empty list counts as empty."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!defaultValue(null, \"Sin asignar\")?","options":["\"Sin asignar\"","true","Un error","null"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!defaultValue devuelve el primer valor no nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!defaultValue(null, \"Unassigned\") return?","options":["\"Unassigned\"","true","An error","null"],"explanation":"a!defaultValue returns the first non-null value."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve left(\"Appian\", 3)?","options":["3","\"Appian\"","\"ian\"","\"App\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"left devuelve los primeros caracteres indicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does left(\"Appian\", 3) return?","options":["3","\"Appian\"","\"ian\"","\"App\""],"explanation":"left returns the first given characters."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve round(3.456, 2)?","options":["3","3.46","3.45","3.5"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"round redondea al número de decimales indicado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does round(3.456, 2) return?","options":["3","3.46","3.45","3.5"],"explanation":"round rounds to the given number of decimals."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve mod(10, 3)?","options":["1","0","3.33","3"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"mod devuelve el resto de la división.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does mod(10, 3) return?","options":["1","0","3.33","3"],"explanation":"mod returns the division remainder."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve upper(\"appian\")?","options":["\"Appian\"","6","\"APPIAN\"","\"appian\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"upper convierte el texto a mayúsculas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does upper(\"appian\") return?","options":["\"Appian\"","6","\"APPIAN\"","\"appian\""],"explanation":"upper converts text to uppercase."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve difference({1, 2, 3, 4}, {2, 4})?","options":["2","{2, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"difference devuelve los elementos de la primera lista que no están en la segunda.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does difference({1, 2, 3, 4}, {2, 4}) return?","options":["2","{2, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}"],"explanation":"difference returns items of the first list not in the second."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve union({1, 2}, {2, 3})?","options":["{1, 2, 2, 3}","{2}","5","{1, 2, 3}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"union combina las listas sin duplicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does union({1, 2}, {2, 3}) return?","options":["{1, 2, 2, 3}","{2}","5","{1, 2, 3}"],"explanation":"union combines lists without duplicates."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla recibe ri!lista = {5, 8, 2} y devuelve a!forEach(items: ri!lista, expression: fv!index). ¿Qué devuelve?","options":["{5, 8, 2}","{1, 2, 3}","15","3"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"fv!index es la posición de cada elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule receives ri!list = {5, 8, 2} and returns a!forEach(items: ri!list, expression: fv!index). What does it return?","options":["{5, 8, 2}","{1, 2, 3}","15","3"],"explanation":"fv!index is each item's position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\"}, expression: upper(fv!item) & fv!index)?","options":["{\"a1\", \"b2\"}","{\"A1\", \"B2\"}","{\"A\", \"B\"}","\"AB12\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Para cada elemento, concatena su mayúscula con su posición.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\"}, expression: upper(fv!item) & fv!index) return?","options":["{\"a1\", \"b2\"}","{\"A1\", \"B2\"}","{\"A\", \"B\"}","\"AB12\""],"explanation":"For each item, it concatenates its uppercase with its position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla devuelve if(a!isNullOrEmpty(ri!nombre), \"Anónimo\", ri!nombre). ¿Cuál es su propósito?","options":["Devolver el nombre o \"Anónimo\" si está vacío","Validar que el nombre tiene un formato correcto","Guardar el nombre en la base de datos","Convertir el nombre a mayúsculas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Proporciona un valor por defecto cuando la entrada está vacía.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule returns if(a!isNullOrEmpty(ri!name), \"Anonymous\", ri!name). What's its purpose?","options":["Return the name, or \"Anonymous\" if empty","Validate the name's format","Save the name to the database","Convert the name to uppercase"],"explanation":"It provides a default when the input is empty."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!localVariables(local!a: 2, local!b: 3, local!a * local!b)?","options":["23","6","{2, 3}","5"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Declara dos variables locales y devuelve su producto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!localVariables(local!a: 2, local!b: 3, local!a * local!b) return?","options":["23","6","{2, 3}","5"],"explanation":"It declares two local variables and returns their product."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve {1, 2, 3} + 1 en Appian?","options":["7","Un error","{2, 3, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 1}"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las operaciones aritméticas con listas se aplican elemento a elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does {1, 2, 3} + 1 return in Appian?","options":["7","An error","{2, 3, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 1}"],"explanation":"Arithmetic with lists applies element by element."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe devolver el nombre completo a partir de nombre y apellidos. ¿Qué implementación es adecuada?","options":["Una constante con el nombre completo de cada usuario","Rule inputs nombre y apellidos y la expresión ri!nombre & \" \" & ri!apellidos","Una consulta a la base de datos por cada llamada","Un process model"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Una regla sencilla con rule inputs concatena los valores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must return a full name from first name and last name. Which implementation fits?","options":["A constant with each user's full name","Rule inputs firstName and lastName with ri!firstName & \" \" & ri!lastName","A database query on every call","A process model"],"explanation":"A simple rule with rule inputs concatenates the values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve isnull(null)?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"isnull indica si el valor es nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does isnull(null) return?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"explanation":"isnull indicates whether the value is null."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve text(7, \"00\")?","options":["\"7.00\"","\"07\"","7","\"00\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"text aplica el formato indicado; \"00\" rellena con ceros a dos dígitos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does text(7, \"00\") return?","options":["\"7.00\"","\"07\"","7","\"00\""],"explanation":"text applies the given format; \"00\" zero-pads to two digits."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve len(\"Appian\")?","options":["1","6","5","\"Appian\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"len devuelve la longitud de un texto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does len(\"Appian\") return?","options":["1","6","5","\"Appian\""],"explanation":"len returns a text's length."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve reverse({1, 2, 3})?","options":["{3, 2, 1}","{1, 2, 3}","3","6"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"reverse invierte el orden de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does reverse({1, 2, 3}) return?","options":["{3, 2, 1}","{1, 2, 3}","3","6"],"explanation":"reverse inverts the list's order."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla de expresión usa ri!fecha y devuelve ri!fecha + 30. ¿Qué devuelve si ri!fecha es 1 de enero de 2026?","options":["Un error, porque no se pueden sumar números a fechas","1 de febrero de 2026","31 de enero de 2026","30"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Sumar un entero a una fecha añade días.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An expression rule uses ri!date and returns ri!date + 30. What does it return if ri!date is January 1, 2026?","options":["An error, because numbers can't be added to dates","February 1, 2026","January 31, 2026","30"],"explanation":"Adding an integer to a date adds days."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {}, expression: fv!item + 1)?","options":["Una lista vacía","{1}","1","null con un error de ejecución"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Con una lista vacía, a!forEach no evalúa la expresión y devuelve una lista vacía.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {}, expression: fv!item + 1) return?","options":["An empty list","{1}","1","null with a runtime error"],"explanation":"With an empty list, a!forEach doesn't evaluate the expression and returns an empty list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve where({true, false, true})?","options":["{2}","{1, 3}","2","{true, true}"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"where devuelve los índices de los valores verdaderos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does where({true, false, true}) return?","options":["{2}","{1, 3}","2","{true, true}"],"explanation":"where returns the indexes of true values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve index({10, 20, 30}, {1, 3}, null)?","options":["{10, 30}","10","{1, 3}","40"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"index admite varios índices y devuelve los elementos correspondientes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index({10, 20, 30}, {1, 3}, null) return?","options":["{10, 30}","10","{1, 3}","40"],"explanation":"index accepts several indexes and returns the matching items."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve index({\"a\", \"b\"}, 5, \"ninguno\")?","options":["\"ninguno\"","\"b\"","null","Un error"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Si el índice no existe, index devuelve el valor por defecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index({\"a\", \"b\"}, 5, \"none\") return?","options":["\"none\"","\"b\"","null","An error"],"explanation":"If the index doesn't exist, index returns the default."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve not(true)?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"not invierte un valor booleano.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does not(true) return?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"explanation":"not inverts a boolean."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador ve en una regla el valor 0.21 escrito directamente en cinco cálculos de IVA. ¿Qué mejora recomienda Appian?","options":["Pedir el valor al usuario cada vez","Escribirlo como texto","Definir el tipo de IVA en una constante y referenciarla","Mantener el número en cada cálculo para que sea más legible"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Evitar valores codificados: las constantes centralizan los valores reutilizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer sees the value 0.21 hard-coded in five VAT calculations in a rule. Which improvement does Appian recommend?","options":["Ask the user for the value every time","Write it as text","Define the VAT rate in a constant and reference it","Keep the number in each calculation so it's more readable"],"explanation":"Avoid hard-coded values: constants centralize reused values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirven los casos de prueba (test cases) de una regla de expresión?","options":["Documentar quién creó la regla","Ejecutar la regla en producción con datos reales cada noche","Mejorar su rendimiento","Guardar entradas y salidas esperadas para comprobar la regla tras cambios"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los test cases verifican que la regla devuelve lo esperado y detectan regresiones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are an expression rule's test cases for?","options":["Documenting who created the rule","Running the rule in production with real data every night","Improving its performance","Storing inputs and expected outputs to check the rule after changes"],"explanation":"Test cases verify the rule returns what's expected and catch regressions."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador cambia una regla usada en 20 objetos. ¿Qué práctica reduce el riesgo de romper algo?","options":["Ejecutar sus casos de prueba y revisar los objetos dependientes","Copiar la regla con otro nombre para cada objeto","No cambiarla nunca","Desplegarla directamente y revisar los errores de los usuarios después"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los test cases y el análisis de dependencias detectan impactos antes de desplegar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer changes a rule used by 20 objects. Which practice reduces the risk of breaking something?","options":["Run its test cases and review dependent objects","Copy the rule under a new name for each object","Never change it","Deploy it directly and review user errors afterwards"],"explanation":"Test cases and dependency analysis catch impact before deployment."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un caso de prueba de una regla tiene entradas definidas, pero no se ha indicado qué debe devolver. ¿Qué se recomienda añadir?","options":["Más rule inputs","Un comentario con el nombre del autor","Una aserción o resultado esperado","Una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las aserciones permiten que el caso de prueba indique si pasa o falla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule's test case has defined inputs but no expected result. What's recommended to add?","options":["More rule inputs","A comment with the author's name","An assertion or expected result","A constant"],"explanation":"Assertions let the test case show whether it passes or fails."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos casos conviene cubrir con test cases en una regla que calcula descuentos? (Elige 2)","options":["Casos límite y entradas nulas","Ningún caso","Solo valores inventados al azar sin resultado esperado","Valores típicos","Solo el caso más frecuente"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Los test cases deben cubrir lo habitual, los límites y las entradas vacías.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two kinds of cases should test cases cover for a discount rule? (Choose 2)","options":["Edge cases and null inputs","No cases","Only random values without expected results","Typical values","Only the most frequent case"],"explanation":"Test cases should cover the typical, the edges and empty inputs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de dato conviene asignar a los rule inputs de una regla?","options":["El tipo concreto esperado (p. ej. Integer, Date, un record type)","Any Type siempre, para que la regla acepte cualquier valor","No asignar tipo","Text siempre"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los tipos concretos evitan errores y documentan la regla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What data type should a rule's rule inputs have?","options":["The specific expected type (e.g. Integer, Date, a record type)","Always Any Type, so the rule accepts any value","No type","Always Text"],"explanation":"Specific types prevent errors and document the rule."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla de expresión tiene 300 líneas que mezclan consultas, cálculos y formato de texto. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Copiarla a cada interfaz","Convertirla en un process model","Añadir comentarios y dejar toda la lógica en la misma regla","Dividirla en reglas más pequeñas con una responsabilidad cada una"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Reglas pequeñas y enfocadas son más fáciles de probar, reutilizar y mantener.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An expression rule has 300 lines mixing queries, calculations and text formatting. Which best practice applies?","options":["Copy it into each interface","Turn it into a process model","Add comments and keep all the logic in one rule","Split it into smaller rules with one responsibility each"],"explanation":"Small, focused rules are easier to test, reuse and maintain."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar a!localVariables dentro de una regla que calcula el mismo valor intermedio varias veces?","options":["Ninguna","Exponer el valor a todas las interfaces","Guardar el valor en la base de datos para otras reglas","Calcularlo una vez y reutilizarlo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las variables locales evitan recalcular expresiones y mejoran la legibilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of using a!localVariables in a rule that computes the same intermediate value several times?","options":["None","Exposing the value to every interface","Saving the value to the database for other rules","Computing it once and reusing it"],"explanation":"Local variables avoid recomputation and improve readability."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {3, 4}, expression: if(fv!item > 3, \"alto\", \"bajo\"))?","options":["\"alto\"","{3, 4}","{\"bajo\", \"alto\"}","{\"alto\", \"bajo\"}"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"3 no es mayor que 3 (\"bajo\"); 4 sí (\"alto\").","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {3, 4}, expression: if(fv!item > 3, \"high\", \"low\")) return?","options":["\"high\"","{3, 4}","{\"low\", \"high\"}","{\"high\", \"low\"}"],"explanation":"3 isn't greater than 3 (\"low\"); 4 is (\"high\")."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve sum(a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * fv!item))?","options":["36","{1, 4, 9}","14","6"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cuadrados son 1, 4 y 9; su suma es 14.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does sum(a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * fv!item)) return?","options":["36","{1, 4, 9}","14","6"],"explanation":"The squares are 1, 4 and 9; their sum is 14."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla recibe una lista de pedidos (record type) y debe devolver solo los importes. ¿Qué expresión es adecuada?","options":["Acceder al campo importe de la lista (p. ej. ri!pedidos[recordType!Pedido.fields.importe])","Una consulta a la base de datos por cada pedido","Una constante","joinarray de los pedidos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Acceder a un campo de una lista devuelve la lista de valores de ese campo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule receives a list of orders (record type) and must return just the amounts. Which expression fits?","options":["Access the amount field of the list (e.g. ri!orders[recordType!Order.fields.amount])","A database query per order","A constant","joinarray of the orders"],"explanation":"Accessing a field of a list returns the list of that field's values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve month(date(2026, 3, 15))?","options":["15","3","2026","\"marzo\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"month devuelve el número de mes de la fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does month(date(2026, 3, 15)) return?","options":["15","3","2026","\"March\""],"explanation":"month returns the date's month number."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve now() frente a today()?","options":["Ninguna devuelve fecha","now() devuelve fecha y hora; today() solo la fecha","today() devuelve fecha y hora; now() solo la hora","Son idénticas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"now() es un Date and Time; today() es un Date.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does now() return compared to today()?","options":["Neither returns a date","now() returns date and time; today() only the date","today() returns date and time; now() only the time","They're identical"],"explanation":"now() is a Date and Time; today() is a Date."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe indicar si un usuario pertenece a un grupo para usarla en showWhen de varias interfaces. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Encapsular la comprobación en una regla reutilizable con el grupo como constante","Crear un proceso","No reutilizar","Escribir el ID del grupo en cada interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Reglas reutilizables y constantes evitan duplicar lógica y valores codificados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must indicate whether a user belongs to a group, for use in showWhen across several interfaces. Which best practice applies?","options":["Encapsulate the check in a reusable rule with the group as a constant","Create a process","Don't reuse","Write the group ID in each interface"],"explanation":"Reusable rules and constants avoid duplicate logic and hard-coded values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla devuelve un error cuando ri!lista es nula y se intenta acceder a su primer elemento. ¿Qué corrección es adecuada?","options":["Exigir que ri!lista nunca sea nula en ningún objeto que la llame","Eliminar el rule input","Usar refreshAlways","Usar index con valor por defecto o comprobar si es nula antes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las reglas robustas gestionan entradas nulas o vacías.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule errors when ri!list is null and it tries to access the first item. Which fix fits?","options":["Require ri!list never to be null in any calling object","Remove the rule input","Use refreshAlways","Use index with a default or check for null first"],"explanation":"Robust rules handle null or empty inputs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3, 4}, expression: if(mod(fv!item, 2) = 0, fv!item, {}))?","options":["6","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}","{2, 4}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Devolver una lista vacía para un elemento lo omite; quedan los pares.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3, 4}, expression: if(mod(fv!item, 2) = 0, fv!item, {})) return?","options":["6","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}","{2, 4}"],"explanation":"Returning an empty list for an item drops it; the even ones remain."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"}, expression: fv!isLast)?","options":["{true, false, false}","{false, false, true}","3","true"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"fv!isLast es verdadero solo en el último elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"}, expression: fv!isLast) return?","options":["{true, false, false}","{false, false, true}","3","true"],"explanation":"fv!isLast is true only on the last item."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve concat(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\")?","options":["\"A B C\"","{\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"}","3","\"ABC\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"concat une los textos sin separador.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does concat(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\") return?","options":["\"A B C\"","{\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"}","3","\"ABC\""],"explanation":"concat joins texts without a separator."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve sum({1, 2}, {3})?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{4, 2}","6","3"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"sum suma todos los valores de sus argumentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does sum({1, 2}, {3}) return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{4, 2}","6","3"],"explanation":"sum adds all values of its arguments."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla calcula una fecha de vencimiento sumando días laborables. ¿Qué función de Appian es útil?","options":["workday","now","today, que también salta fines de semana","len"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"workday suma días laborables a una fecha según el calendario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule computes a due date by adding business days. Which Appian function helps?","options":["workday","now","today, which also skips weekends","len"],"explanation":"workday adds business days to a date per the calendar."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos buenas prácticas recomienda Appian para las reglas de expresión? (Elige 2)","options":["Gestionar entradas nulas","Descripción clara y rule inputs con nombres significativos","Reglas enormes con todo dentro","Valores codificados repetidos","Nombres genéricos como \"regla1\""],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Documentar, nombrar bien y gestionar nulos hacen las reglas robustas y mantenibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two best practices does Appian recommend for expression rules? (Choose 2)","options":["Handling null inputs","Clear description and meaningful rule input names","Huge rules containing everything","Repeated hard-coded values","Generic names like \"rule1\""],"explanation":"Documenting, naming well and handling nulls make rules robust and maintainable."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve if(isnull(ri!x), 0, ri!x * 2) cuando ri!x es 4?","options":["4","8","null","0"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"ri!x no es nulo, así que devuelve 4 × 2.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does if(isnull(ri!x), 0, ri!x * 2) return when ri!x is 4?","options":["4","8","null","0"],"explanation":"ri!x isn't null, so it returns 4 × 2."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve insert({\"a\", \"c\"}, \"b\", 2)?","options":["{\"a\", \"c\", \"b\"}","\"abc\"","{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}","{\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"}"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"insert coloca el valor en la posición indicada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does insert({\"a\", \"c\"}, \"b\", 2) return?","options":["{\"a\", \"c\", \"b\"}","\"abc\"","{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}","{\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"}"],"explanation":"insert places the value at the given position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve remove({10, 20, 30}, 2)?","options":["{30}","{10, 30}","{20}","{10, 20}"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"remove elimina el elemento en la posición indicada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does remove({10, 20, 30}, 2) return?","options":["{30}","{10, 30}","{20}","{10, 20}"],"explanation":"remove deletes the item at the given position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla de expresión consulta datos con a!queryRecordType y se llama desde una interfaz en cada fila de una cuadrícula. ¿Qué riesgo tiene?","options":["Que se borra la cuadrícula","Una consulta por fila, con impacto en rendimiento","Ninguno, porque las reglas se ejecutan en paralelo sin coste","Que no devuelve datos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Llamar a reglas con consultas en cada fila multiplica las consultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An expression rule queries data with a!queryRecordType and is called from an interface on every grid row. What's the risk?","options":["The grid is deleted","One query per row, hurting performance","None, since rules run in parallel at no cost","It returns no data"],"explanation":"Calling query rules on every row multiplies queries."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve displayvalue(2, {1, 2, 3}, {\"Bajo\", \"Medio\", \"Alto\"}, \"N/A\")?","options":["2","\"N/A\"","\"Bajo\"","\"Medio\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"displayvalue busca el valor en la primera lista y devuelve el correspondiente de la segunda.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does displayvalue(2, {1, 2, 3}, {\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\"}, \"N/A\") return?","options":["2","\"N/A\"","\"Low\"","\"Medium\""],"explanation":"displayvalue finds the value in the first list and returns the matching one from the second."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {2, 3}, expression: a!localVariables(local!doble: fv!item * 2, local!doble + 1))?","options":["{3, 4}","{5, 7}","12","{4, 6}"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Para 2: 4 + 1 = 5; para 3: 6 + 1 = 7.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {2, 3}, expression: a!localVariables(local!double: fv!item * 2, local!double + 1)) return?","options":["{3, 4}","{5, 7}","12","{4, 6}"],"explanation":"For 2: 4 + 1 = 5; for 3: 6 + 1 = 7."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere interpretar qué hace una regla heredada sin documentación. ¿Qué es lo más útil?","options":["Desplegarla en producción para ver cómo se comporta con usuarios","Probarla con distintas entradas en el editor y revisar sus casos de prueba","Preguntar en el AppMarket","Borrarla y reescribirla"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Probar entradas y revisar test cases ayuda a entender el comportamiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to understand what an undocumented legacy rule does. What's most useful?","options":["Deploy it to production to see how it behaves with users","Test it with various inputs in the editor and review its test cases","Ask in the AppMarket","Delete and rewrite it"],"explanation":"Testing inputs and reviewing test cases help understand behavior."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve tointeger(\"42\") + 1?","options":["\"421\"","Un error","42","43"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"tointeger convierte el texto a entero; luego se suma 1.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does tointeger(\"42\") + 1 return?","options":["\"421\"","An error","42","43"],"explanation":"tointeger converts text to an integer; then 1 is added."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item)[2]?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","2","3","1"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El resultado es la lista {1, 2, 3}; el índice 2 devuelve 2.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item)[2] return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","2","3","1"],"explanation":"The result is the list {1, 2, 3}; index 2 returns 2."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla que devuelve el estado traducido de una solicitud usa una cadena de 8 if anidados. ¿Qué alternativa es más legible?","options":["a!match o una decisión","Un process model","Añadir más if anidados con comentarios","Una consulta por cada estado"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!match o un decision object simplifican múltiples casos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule returning a request's translated status uses a chain of 8 nested ifs. Which alternative is more readable?","options":["a!match or a decision","A process model","More nested ifs with comments","A query per status"],"explanation":"a!match or a decision object simplifies multiple cases."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos funciones devuelven valores de fecha? (Elige 2)","options":["len(\"texto\")","upper(\"a\")","sum({1})","date(2026, 1, 15)","today()"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"today y date devuelven fechas; las demás, números o texto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two functions return date values? (Choose 2)","options":["len(\"text\")","upper(\"a\")","sum({1})","date(2026, 1, 15)","today()"],"explanation":"today and date return dates; the others return numbers or text."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}, expression: fv!isFirst)?","options":["true","{false, false, true}","{true, false, false}","1"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"fv!isFirst es verdadero solo en el primer elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}, expression: fv!isFirst) return?","options":["true","{false, false, true}","{true, false, false}","1"],"explanation":"fv!isFirst is true only on the first item."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve min({8, 3, 5})?","options":["8","5","16","3"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"min devuelve el valor más bajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does min({8, 3, 5}) return?","options":["8","5","16","3"],"explanation":"min returns the lowest value."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe devolver true si una solicitud tiene importe mayor que 0 y un responsable asignado. ¿Qué expresión es correcta?","options":["isnull(ri!responsable)","ri!importe > 0","or(ri!importe > 0, isnull(ri!responsable))","and(ri!importe > 0, not(isnull(ri!responsable)))"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"and exige ambas condiciones; el responsable no debe ser nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must return true if a request has an amount over 0 and an assigned owner. Which expression is correct?","options":["isnull(ri!owner)","ri!amount > 0","or(ri!amount > 0, isnull(ri!owner))","and(ri!amount > 0, not(isnull(ri!owner)))"],"explanation":"and requires both conditions; the owner must not be null."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere usar la misma lógica de cálculo en una interfaz, en un process model y en una Web API. ¿Dónde la coloca?","options":["En la interfaz, y la copia en el proceso y en la Web API","En una constante","En un grupo","En una regla de expresión que llaman los tres"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las reglas de expresión son reutilizables desde interfaces, procesos y Web APIs.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants the same calculation logic in an interface, a process model and a Web API. Where do they put it?","options":["In the interface, copied into the process and the Web API","In a constant","In a group","In an expression rule all three call"],"explanation":"Expression rules are reusable from interfaces, processes and Web APIs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve right(\"2026-ABC\", 3)?","options":["\"ABC\"","3","\"202\"","\"6-A\""],"correct":[0],"explanation":"right devuelve los últimos caracteres indicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does right(\"2026-ABC\", 3) return?","options":["\"ABC\"","3","\"202\"","\"6-A\""],"explanation":"right returns the last given characters."}}}]}$exam$::jsonb);
    raise notice 'Examen appian-associate-developer añadido con 500 preguntas.';
  end if;
end
$do$;

select e.code, d.code as dominio, d.name, count(q.id) as preguntas
from public.exams e
join public.domains d on d.exam_id = e.id
left join public.questions q on q.domain_id = d.id
where e.slug = 'appian-associate-developer'
group by e.code, d.code, d.name
order by d.code;
